y’s structure. And that’s why the physical therapy that looks like “just fixing legs” is also secretly fixing the hidden core problem. I’m not asking you to trust a complex nerve map. I’m just saying that when your aunt sees a patient with spaghetti legs after a belly surgery, the simplest, most truthful summary might be: “Their trunk is shot, so their legs forgot how to work.” No medical jargon needed.
